				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync editor element submodules for SCM protocol alignment and build stability\n\nUpdate all tracked editor element submodules (Cocoon, Common, Maintain, Mountain, Sky) to their latest revisions on the Current branch to resolve Source Control Management (SCM) payload deserialization issues and harden the build pipeline.\n\n**Specific Changes:**\n- **Cocoon:** Fix the `update_scm_group` RPC call payload to use `providerId` and `groupId` instead of non-standard `scmHandle` fields, ensuring alignment with `Vine.proto` definitions.\n- **Common:** Make `ProviderHandle` optional in Source Control DTOs (`SourceControlGroupUpdateDTO`) to support flexible serialization where the handle is passed positionally.\n- **Mountain:** Prevent Tauri build failures by generating a stub `extensions.manifest.json` if missing, and refine the `UpdateScmGroup` logic to emit correct `scmId` events for the Sky frontend. Additionally, extend the extension descriptor cache lifetime to 24 hours to reduce redundant rescans.\n- **Sky:** Integrate new Astro build integrations for baking the extension manifest at compile-time and compressing the bundle with Brotli, reducing runtime overhead and distribution size.\n- **Maintain:** Consolidate lint suppressions in `build.rs` to match the main crate strategy and reduce build noise.\n\nThese changes ensure the SCM group updates function correctly across the Mountain-Cocoon-Sky IPC boundary while optimizing the application startup sequence and build reliability.",
			"SHA": "19ae8e1a8b650e16de7e0837a317a1915a5a6f8c"
		},
