				8
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update editor element submodules to consolidate build script lint allowances\n\nSync all tracked editor element submodules (Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Maintain, Mountain, Rest, SideCar) to their latest revisions on the Current branch. The primary focus is the centralization of lint suppression directives (`non_snake_case`, `dead_code`, `unused_*`) into `build.rs` files across Rust-based submodules.\n\nThis follows the recent enforcement of strict PascalCase naming in source modules by moving blanket allowances out of `Source/` directories. The build scripts now handle warnings generated by build-time metadata, external FFI bindings, and auto-generated code, ensuring the main application source remains clean and warning-free. Maintain also aligns its `Library.rs` to suppress `dead_code` at the crate level for stub implementations.\n\nThese changes unify the linting strategy across the backend ecosystem, preventing build noise during refactoring while maintaining the project's strict naming conventions for functional code.",
			"SHA": "f42c11645c7091e7f4bbfb9d07bfa76c836c62b1"
		}
